hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21041","Rawh narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Hudayn Abu Sasan al-Raqashi, from al-Muhajir ibn Qunfudh ibn Umayr ibn Judan, he said: I greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was performing ablution, and he did not return it to me. When he finished his ablution, he said: nothing prevented me from returning it to you except that I was without ablution."
"21042","Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Said, and Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Hudayn Abu Sasan, from al-Muhajir ibn Qunfudh, Abd al-Wahhab said: ibn Umayr ibn Judan, that he greeted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was performing ablution, and he did not return it to him. When he finished his ablution, he said: nothing prevented me from returning it to you except that I disliked remembering Allah, blessed and exalted is He, except in a state of purity."
"21043","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from al-Muhajir ibn Qunfudh, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was urinating, or had urinated, and I greeted him, and he did not return it to me until he performed ablution, then he returned it to me."
"21044","Arim narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, he said: and my father narrated, from Abu al-Ala ibn Umayr al-Jurayri, he said: I was with Qatadah ibn Milhan when he was dying, and a man passed in the far part of the house, he said: then I saw him in the face of Qatadah, he said: and whenever I saw him, it was as if oil was on his face, he said: and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had wiped his face."
"21045","Yahya ibn Main and Huraym ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, they said: Mutamir narrated to us, he said: my father said, from Abu al-Ala ibn Umayr: I was with Qatadah ibn Milhan, then he mentioned similar to it."
